From d95106256bc35396086e8075344d54a98414918a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fountain5405 <Fountain5405@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:59:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/11] fcmp_pp: verify a batch in two steps, prepare per batch
 and one finish per call

fcmp_pp_verify checks one batch end to end: the per-proof checks, the
ed25519 batch check, then one multiexp per curve. So that a caller can
merge the multiexps of several batches, the FFI now also offers the steps
separately:

- fcmp_pp_verify_prepare runs one batch's per-proof checks and its ed25519
  check, exactly as fcmp_pp_verify does, and returns the batch's Selene and
  Helios verifier state, or null if any check fails;
- fcmp_pp_verify_finish merges all states (BatchVerifier::merge) and runs
  one multiexp per curve, split over up to `split` threads
  (Generators::verify_split). It consumes every state, whatever the result;
- destroy_fcmp_pp_batch_state frees a state that never reached finish.

The C++ wrappers in prove.h/prove.cpp are verify_prepare, verify_finish
(which sets the consumed pointers to nullptr) and batch_state_free.
fcmp_pp_verify is unchanged, and nothing calls the new functions yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
